A||||8||86SE||Flexplate Question||||1||
Z||000000||86SE||09-20-2000||10:11 PM||||I am doing a 3.4L engine conversion and the 3.4's are internally balanced and they require a '88 Fiero 2.8 Flywheel.  I also heard to get the automatic transmission to bolt up to the engine, you just need a flexplate from an auto 2.8 Fiero (1988).<P>Does the flexplate just bolt up to the flywheel?? And will it solve all the balancing problems with the 2 eninges being differently balanced??<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000001||86SE||09-20-2000||10:38 PM||||Wait a minute.  Is a flexplate just a flywheel for automatic transmissions??<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||5
Z||000002||rprevo||09-20-2000||10:40 PM|||| The first thing you should do is call a<BR>balance shop and get there oppinion.<BR>I may be wrong but it seems like every once<BR>in a while you'll find a guy that really<BR>understands what your trying to do and can<BR>get you there, Also don't be afraid of a seconed oppinion.<BR> Ray||||reg||6
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||09-21-2000||06:57 PM||||Flexplate, Flywheel, same thing. Clutch plate different!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sarlacc||09-21-2000||10:36 PM||||A flexplate and a flywheel are not the same thing!  A flexplate is used on an automatic transmission, designed to flex, which is what the name implies.  A flywheel is used on a manual transmission, does not flex, and has a machined surface where it contacts the clutch disc.||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||09-21-2000||11:45 PM||||Thanks guys! Thats what I needed to know.||||reg||10
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||09-22-2000||03:15 AM||||OOps! I stand corrected. Teach me to be on here when frustrated and tired.<BR>Rephrase: Clutch plate, Flywheel same thing. Flex plate different.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||09-22-2000||03:15 AM||||OOps! I stand corrected. Teach me to be on here when frustrated and tired.<BR>Rephrase: Clutch plate, Flywheel same thing. Flex plate different.<BR>Thanx Sarlacc||||reg||1
Z||000008||Sarlacc||09-22-2000||12:19 PM||||No problem Indiana, and as far a posting eroneously due to exhaustion goes : been there, done that, bought the t-shirt factory. :-)||||reg||1
